EXT. ROOFTOP WATER TANK - SUBURBAN NIGHT

A wooden tank on stilts above a flat tar roof. Cicadas. A radio plays low from an open window below.

SADIE KOWALSKI-IBRAHIM, 16, sits on the ledge with her feet dangling. Her younger cousin MILO BERGSTROM, 13, climbs the last rung of the ladder, breathless. He freezes when he sees her. She doesn't turn.

He climbs onto the roof. She hears him. Shifts a few inches to make room. He sits. They stare at the neighbors' lit windows.

RADIO (V.O.)
(muffled, from below)
...and now, the late-night countdown. Number three this week...

She hums along. He taps his heel against the brick. A long moment passes.

He offers her a cracker from his pocket. She takes it. They chew in the dark.

She shoves him gently. He shoves back. She nearly slides off the ledge; he grabs her sleeve. They both go still. Then she laughs, and he lets go, and neither of them says what almost happened.

RADIO (V.O.)
...and the number one song in the country...

She stands, brushes crumbs from her knees. Holds out her hand. He takes it. They climb down together, the song swelling behind them.
